      "typeVersion": 3.5
    },
    {
      "id": "da40e264-ec63-488a-907c-ad7ed20f05bf",
      "name": "GitHub Pages Setup Instructions1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        7280,
        1664
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 496,
        "height": 544,
        "content": "### GitHub Pages hosting setup\n1. Create a public GitHub repository to hold the generated form pages (or reuse one you already host with Pages).\n2. In the repo, go to Settings -> Pages and enable Pages, deploying from the branch/folder you'll commit to (these nodes commit to \"main\" by default - change the branch in both GitHub nodes below if you use a different one, e.g. \"gh-pages\").\n3. Create a GitHub Personal Access Token with repo access, then add a GitHub credential in n8n and attach it to Check If File Exists and both Publish to GitHub Pages nodes.\n4. Open the GitHub Hosting Config node (right after Chat Trigger) and replace YOUR_GITHUB_USERNAME and YOUR_PAGES_REPO with your real GitHub username/org and repo name. Every GitHub node's Owner/Repository and the hostedUrl in Compose Hosted URL read from this one node, so you only fill it in once.\n5. Get Public Form HTML calls SubmitRax's API to fetch the form's public HTML - confirm the endpoint path against SubmitRax's API docs and adjust the URL if needed; it reuses the same Bearer token credential as the MCP node.\n\n### The hosted URL link tak ea while to go live. Be patient!"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
